.TH SDL_HINT_MAC_USE_GCMOUSE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_MAC_USE_GCMOUSE \- A variable controlling whether the GCMouse API will be used on macOS.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_MAC_USE_GCMOUSE \(dqSDL_MAC_USE_GCMOUSE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
On supported versions of macOS, GCMouse is usually a better way to read mouse input, but may cause problems in some scenarios (remote control software that wants to send non-GCMouse input events, etc)\[char46]
.PP
When GCMouse is disabled, SDL will use standard Cocoa mouse events\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: GCMouse won\(aqt be used\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: GCMouse will be used if available\[char46] (default)
.PP
This hint needs to be set before
.BR SDL_Init ()\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

